pmg-gui (5.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * spam quarantine: allow marking mails as seen, via a context-menu action,
    the 's' shortcut and a toolbar toggle button, so users of a shared mailbox
    can flag a processed mail without deleting it. Seen mails are marked
    inline in the Sender/Subject column.

  * quarantine: load external images on demand through a tri-state image
    selector (show all, on-demand, hide) and a "Load Images" button, which is
    only revealed when the opened mail actually references external resources.

  * spam quarantine: show the net spam score together with the summed positive
    and negative test scores, to better judge borderline mails.

  * quarantine views: widen the default mail list region to fit more of the
    sender and subject without resizing, making better use of modern (bigger)
    display sizes.

  * dashboard: add a "Top Senders" panel next to the existing "Top Receivers"
    one.

  * dashboard: HTML-encode the recipient address in the "Top Receivers" panel
    to prevent injecting markup into the admin dashboard through a crafted
    recipient.

  * mail tracker: make the result limit configurable, so a query is no longer
    silently capped at 2000 entries.

  * cluster: assist node joining via copyable join information, decoding a
    pasted blob into the peer address and fingerprint and checking it against
    the local node's product and release.

  * cluster: avoid logging out the user during a cluster join, which
    previously failed mid-join once the synced authentication key invalidated
    the current session.

